presetShapeDefinitions.xml in this folder is a file of ECMA-376, Office Open
XML File Formats, Part 1, 5th edition (December 2016). Ecma International
holds its copyright. ivy keeps the file byte for byte, and it does not change
it. The package drawingml generates its tables of the preset shapes from it
(D24).

Source:
  https://ecma-international.org/publications-and-standards/standards/ecma-376/
  https://ecma-international.org/wp-content/uploads/ECMA-376-1_5th_edition_december_2016.zip
  The ZIP holds OfficeOpenXML-DrawingMLGeometries.zip, and that ZIP holds
  presetShapeDefinitions.xml.

SHA-256:
  9d0bcad9cf06054785b03762fcfadbf6bab7e54a5f9d69434e34b7fd464d4129  ECMA-376-1_5th_edition_december_2016.zip
  a8517838a3a60492d267d1ff92e1ebd831adc04584de79a38a5532a68902abf6  OfficeOpenXML-DrawingMLGeometries.zip
  2f7c868d857c1e3c4b5a6068759fe0e07d77ad58377a6618d1b02ba3507b6939  presetShapeDefinitions.xml

The text of Part 1 does not print a copyright notice. The Ecma text copyright
policy, version 3 (approved in December 2025), says that the default notice
below applies to the older standards too. The policy is at
https://ecma-international.org/wp-content/uploads/Ecma_text_copyright_policy_version_3.pdf
and its SHA-256 is
2dcbec958059c8b512b6798ee1f0b8416c33d507a21f5bd9a20c19e68218776f.

The file has these errors that ivy knows of:

1. It holds the shape upDownArrow twice, with the same text. The generator
   of the package keeps one.
2. It does not hold the shape upArrow. The generator adds an upArrow that
   ivy wrote as the mirror image of downArrow.
3. The text rectangle of pie has t="ir" and r="it". The generator swaps
   them.
4. Eight guides of circularArrow, leftCircularArrow and
   leftRightCircularArrow have one argument too many, such as
   "+- xH 0 dxB 0". The package skips the extra argument.

